##grflangid 0x00
STR_GRF_NAME	:Mount Washington Cog Railway - Alpha
STR_GRF_DESCRIPTION	:The engines of the Mount Washington Cog Railway in New Hampshire, United States.

STR_PARAM_DISABLESPEEDER_NAME	:Disable worker service vehicles
STR_PARAM_DISABLESPEEDER_DESC	:Enable/Disable vehicles for worker service use.{}Specifically the Devil's Shingle and the Hornet.{}These engines as implemented do not accept wagons and have minimal passenger capacity, making these engines more eyecandy than useful.
STR_PARAM_DISABLEPROTOTYPE_NAME	:Disable prototype vehicles
STR_PARAM_DISABLEPROTOTYPE_DESC	:Enable/Disable vehicles that were built, but not used in service.{}Specifically the Spirit.

STR_PARAM_DATES_NAME	:Vehicle Start Dates
STR_PARAM_DATES_DESC	:By default, vehicles' start dates and model life are aligned with the time it was built in reality. This means that several vehicles expire before the default 1950 game start date. The scaled option changes vehicle's start dates to be more appropriate for a game in that date range.
STR_PARAM_DATES_VALUE_REAL	:Real dates (Starting 1866)
STR_PARAM_DATES_VALUE_TOY	:Scaled to 1950-2050

STR_PEPPERSASS_NAME	:Peppersass
STR_SHINGLE_NAME	:Devil's Shingle
STR_HORIZONTALBOILER_NAME	:Hercules
STR_SPIRIT_NAME	:Spirit
STR_DIESEL_NAME	:Wajo Nanatasis
STR_SPEEDER_NAME	:Hornet

STR_PASSENGER_NAME	:Passenger Car
STR_FLATCAR_NAME	:Flatcar

STR_ERROR_CANNOT_ATTACH_ANY	:Wagons cannot be attached to this engine.
